# Claude Code workflow reference

Env-specific facts and decisions, each dated; decisions and their triggers live in the chezmoi
repo's `docs/decisions.md`. If behavior seems changed, verify (claude-code-guide) and update.

## Models (last verified 2026-09-25)

- Settings pin the driver (`model` key) to `{{ index .subagent_tiers.claude .agents.claude.defaults.tier }}`;
  effort `{{ .agents.claude.defaults.reasoning_effort }}` is pinned under `modelSettings` for every pin with an
  effort knob, so a `/model` escalation keeps it. The 1M window is the default on the current pins (no `[1m]` suffix).
- Escalate effort first: `/effort xhigh` keeps the prompt cache. `{{ .subagent_tiers.claude.frontier }}`
  is escalation-only (since 2026-09-25): for an ambiguous root-cause or architecture problem
  where the driver at higher effort fell short, start a fresh session with
  `claude --model {{ .subagent_tiers.claude.frontier }}`. Do not `/model` a grown session: each model has its own
  cache, so the next request re-reads the whole history uncached at the frontier rate, and
  `/model <name>` saves it as the default until the next apply (decision 2026-09-26). In a
  frontier-model session don't fork and don't run workflows — forks inherit it, and a workflow
  `agent({model:'fable'})` has no guard.
- Roles render from `subagents` in agents.yaml; `docs/decisions.md` records each why. Pins do not
  follow `/model`; a child without explicit effort inherits session effort.

